    id: "aspect",
    title: "Aspect: imperfective and perfective",
    blurb: "Choose between \"was doing\" and \"got it done\", in the past and in the future.",
    deck: "Work and study",
    body: `
<p>English has "I read", "I was reading" and "I have read". Russian has fewer tenses, but almost every verb comes as a pair: an <b>imperfective</b> and a <b>perfective</b>. This choice is called aspect.</p>
<h3>Imperfective: the process or the habit</h3>
<p>Use the imperfective for an action in progress, for something repeated, or just to name the activity. All the verbs you have used so far are imperfective, so you already know half of every pair.</p>
{{ex:Каждый день я читаю.|KAHZH-dihy dyehn' yah chee-TAH-yoo|I read every day.}}
{{ex:Вчера вечером я читал.|fchih-RAH VYEH-chih-rahm yah chee-TAHL|Last night I was reading. (a man)}}
<h3>Perfective: one finished result</h3>
<p>Use the perfective for one action that was completed, with a result. Most perfectives add a prefix; a few are different words.</p>
<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>Imperfective</th><th>Perfective</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class="k">читать</td><td class="k">прочитать</td><td>read</td></tr><tr><td class="k">делать</td><td class="k">сделать</td><td>do, make</td></tr><tr><td class="k">писать</td><td class="k">написать</td><td>write</td></tr><tr><td class="k">покупать</td><td class="k">купить</td><td>buy</td></tr></table></div>
{{ex:Я прочитал книгу.|yah prah-chee-TAHL KNEE-goo|I finished reading the book. (a man)}}
{{ex:Она написала письмо.|ah-NAH nah-pee-SAH-lah pees'-MOH|She wrote the letter.}}
<h3>Ask one question: did it get done?</h3>
<p>If the point is the finished result, choose the perfective. If the point is the activity itself, how long it went on or how often, choose the imperfective. The past endings agree with the subject in both: <b>сделал</b>, <b>сделала</b>, <b>сделали</b>.</p>
{{ex:Вчера я делала домашнее задание.|fchih-RAH yah DYEH-lah-lah dah-MAHSH-nih-yih zah-DAH-nee-yih|Yesterday I was doing my homework. (a woman)}}
{{ex:Я сделала домашнее задание.|yah ZDYEH-lah-lah dah-MAHSH-nih-yih zah-DAH-nee-yih|I've done my homework. (a woman)}}
<h3>The future</h3>
<p>The imperfective future is <b>буду</b> + infinitive: <b>Я буду читать</b>. The perfective has no <b>буду</b>: its present-type endings already mean the future. <b>Я прочитаю</b> is "I'll read it (to the end)", and <b>я куплю</b> is "I'll buy".</p>
{{ex:Завтра я куплю хлеб.|ZAHF-trah yah koo-PLYOO khlyehp|Tomorrow I'll buy bread.}}
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> a perfective for a habit. <b>Каждый день я купил хлеб</b> → <b>Каждый день я покупал хлеб</b>. And never <b>Я буду прочитать</b>: say <b>Я прочитаю</b> or <b>Я буду читать</b>. Read the Cyrillic first, and use the respelling only to check the stress.</div>
`,
